Hints::readTables() allocates a std::vector<char> of hintsLength +
hintsLength2, the lengths the linearization dictionary names in /H, before
it reads the hint tables from the file. Nothing bounds them: a ~1 KB file
with /H [offset 2000000000] makes it zero-fill a 2 GB buffer (bad_alloc
abort on the 512 MB wasm heap, 2 GB RSS natively), only for the read to run
into EOF a few bytes later. PDFDoc::getPage() reaches it through
checkLinearization() for any document with a /Linearized dictionary.

Refuse hint table lengths larger than the file before allocating: such a
table cannot be read from it (the substream ends at the end of the base
stream), so this changes no outcome, only skips the allocation. Regression
test cpp/tests/poppler-hints-length-test.cpp fails every operator new above
256 MB.

Not fixed upstream as of d50f45b.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and open MRs searched for
Hints, hintsLength).

